A||N||29||Haze_Performance||My visit to the Autoparts store (Kinda Long) ||||8||
Z||000000||Haze_Performance||03-02-2001||04:20 PM||||So for some reason the ignition in the 87 locked up yesterday. (the key wouldn't turn) So I went to my neighborhood Trac Auto.<P><B>Counter lady</B> Can I help you?<P><B>Me</B> Yes, I need a an ignition lock & key set for a 1987 Pontiac Fiero.<P><B>Counter lady</B> Tilt?<P><B>Me</B> Yes.<P><B>Counter lady</B> Column or Counsel Shifter?<P><B>Me</B> Column?? They don't come in Column Shift!!??<P><B>Counter lady</B> Yes they do.. I've seen them..<P><B>Me</B> In a PONTIAC FIERO huh?<P><B>Counter lady</B> Yes.. Which one is it...<P><B>Me</B> (<I>Grrrrr..</I>) It only comes it Counsel Shift & thats what it is.<P><B>Counter lady</B> Ok...but I've seen it in Column.<P><B>Me</B> (<I>Grrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrr......</I>)  <P>Counter lady walks away. Comes back and hands me a part.<P><B>Counter lady</B> Here you go.<P><B>Me</B> (opening the box) This is an ignition switch. Not a ignition lock & key set. (<I>Vein starting to tremble on forehead</I>)<P><B>Counter lady</B> Lets see...Oh be right back.<P>Counter lady walks away. Comes back and hands me another part.<P><B>Me</B> (opening the box) This is an ignition lock & key set for a Ford!! Hence the Ford key sticking in it!! (<I>Vein on forehead has now popped</I>)<P><B>Counter lady</B> Thats what it calls for...<P><B>Me</B> The box even says FORD on it!!!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> This isn't it!!!!<P><B>Counter lady</B> Be right back.<P>Counter lady walks away. Comes back and hands me yet another part.<P><B>Me</B> (opening the box) This is a Lexus part!!! (<I>AHHHHH!!!!, BANG-BANG-BANG-BANG-BANG-BANG-BANG-BANG- reload -BANG-BANG-BANG-BANG-BANG-BANG</I>) What's the problem!?!? I need the LOCK & KEY SET FOR A PONTIAC FIERO!!!!! <P><B>Counter lady</B> Ohh..Be right back.<P>Counter lady walks away. She yells back to me.. We have 2 kinds. Black & Chrome. What one do you want?<P><B>Me</B> BRING THEM BOTH!!!!!! (<I>Now I know why we cant carry concealed weapons in Illinois...I would have killed her long ago.</I>)<P>Counter comes back and hands me the 2 parts.<P><B>Me</B> (<I>Thank God they look right</I>) How much??!!<BR> <BR><B>Counter lady</B> $17.99 for Chrome - $27.99 for Black.<P><B>Me</B> $27.99 for Black??!! Doesn't that seem alittle high to you??!!<P><B>Counter lady</B> Yes thats our price.<P>I grab the black one and head to the checkout. <I>I know it cant be $27.99.</I><P>The Checkout guy scans it and its only $15.99...(<I>Ahhhhhh!!!! BANG-BANG-BANG-BANG-BANG-BANG-BANG!!!!</I>)<P>WHY ARE THESE PEOPLE TORTURING ME??!!!<P>I was so happy to get out of there... I was out of imaginary bullets.. lol  <P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank><BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ttttttt.gif">  </A>       <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>PFF Members Photo Page</A><BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1431213" TARGET=_blank><BR>Photopoint Gallery (Updated Weekly)</A>||||reg||8
Z||000001||danny boy||03-02-2001||04:44 PM|||| If you think thats bad, you should try getting parts at the Advance we have here. I swear that most auto parts stores shift through applications and hire THE DUMBEST PEOPLE THEY CAN FIND!!!<BR>  Hey, did you ever find a dash?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||bHooper||03-02-2001||04:55 PM||||i have to say, that i have been fortunate in my dealings with Advance Auto and AutoZone.  Between Bob Englert's 4 cars (now 3), mine and some other "mystery person" that supposedly is building kit cars, we have a well informed AutoZone to work with.<P>of course, that still doesnt keep them from looking at you like your an idiot for having a fiero... it just means they know what parts to work with.<P>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000003||stimpy||03-02-2001||05:01 PM||||Last time at Autozone, I asked for a windshield washer pump for an 86 Fiero. "Four cylinder or six?"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>But it definately sounds like your counter(productive) lady takes the cake!||||reg||1
Z||000004||Haze_Performance||03-02-2001||05:03 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by danny boy:<BR><B>   Hey, did you ever find a dash?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Not yet...Still looking..I have a few members on the look out.. <BR><P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank><BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ttttttt.gif">  </A>       <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>PFF Members Photo Page</A><BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1431213" TARGET=_blank><BR>Photopoint Gallery (Updated Weekly)</A>||||reg||7
Z||000005||Racer 1||03-02-2001||05:38 PM||||This is what pisses me off the most. I go into autozone theres three lines formed to get help at the computers. I wait in one line that has a guy that has skillz in automotive parts knowledge. I get down to the counter and the guy has to help checkout. Then I get the dumb dude that doesnt know jack about a fiero. It takes him 20 minutes to get my part do to him answering like 50 phone calls. But the autozone lady who was checking me out had a nice chest and butt so that took my mind off the last past 30 minutes. <P>Another thing sometimes when I call down there to AutoZone they put me on hold forever never picked the phone back up.<P>And always make sure you have the right part before leaving like on clutch rear master cyld. Sometimes there different!<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=159982&a=1168563&p=42189251&Sequence=0"> ||||reg||13
Z||000006||Predator||03-02-2001||05:53 PM||||My wife went to a Pep Boys and got them to install the part. The guy at the counter asked for her name. She said Georgia. The guy asks how do you spell that? The reason this is funny is we live in Georgia. The guy didn't know how to spell the state he lives in  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero4_1.jpg"> ||||reg||7
Z||000007||sqoach||03-02-2001||05:54 PM||||haze, i'm replacing my ignition lock thingy too. i've gotten all the way down to the lock plate, but can't get it off of there. i know there's a special tool to use to get that off of there. when you get it installed, just give an update as to how difficult it was to do. thanks.<P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mysig2.JPG"> <BR>84 SE (project car?)<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)<BR>86 SC (daily driver)||||reg||1
Z||000008||Oreif||03-02-2001||06:09 PM||||LOL LOL<BR>Haze, that has got to be one of the funniest encounters I've read. Sorry you had a hard time. I just wish the guy at Trak Auto by my house would quit calling it a Buick Fiero!||||reg||1
Z||000009||Haze_Performance||03-02-2001||06:23 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by sqoach:<BR><B>haze, i'm replacing my ignition lock thingy too. i've gotten all the way down to the lock plate, but can't get it off of there. i know there's a special tool to use to get that off of there. when you get it installed, just give an update as to how difficult it was to do. thanks.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>You need a Lock Plate removal tool.. I picked one up at NAPPA Auto Parts for $15.00. Its VERY easy to use.<BR><P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank><BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ttttttt.gif">  </A>       <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>PFF Members Photo Page</A><BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1431213" TARGET=_blank><BR>Photopoint Gallery (Updated Weekly)</A>||||reg||14
