Z||000011||Raydar||03-02-2001||11:02 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Predator:<BR><B>My wife went to a Pep Boys and got them to install the part. The guy at the counter asked for her name. She said Georgia. The guy asks how do you spell that? The reason this is funny is we live in Georgia. The guy didn't know how to spell the state he lives in    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Many of the folks who work at Pep Boys couldn't find their butts with both hands.<BR>The guy who sold me my 88 coupe was a Pep Boys mechanic. I bought it anyway, though.<BR>I could tell you several horror stories about Pep Boys brake jobs. <I>Parts falling out,   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> etc.</I><P>Haze. Been there. Understand completely.<P><BR>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 03-02-2001).]||||reg||1
