Z||000017||kslish||03-03-2001||04:13 PM||||I see Trak Auto is still the same as it was when they had stores in the Pittsburgh area.  They all went out of business here a few years back.  <P>Ken S.<BR>'87 GT and '86 SC<BR> <A HREF="http://www.westpennfiero.org" TARGET=_blank>www.westpennfiero.org</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000018||Black88GT||03-03-2001||04:27 PM||||Oh man I could tell you guys many many Pep Boys horror stories.  My friend works there doing oil changes.  He said sometimes the new people they hire forget to put oil back in the car after they have taken it out (more then one occasion), needless to say the customers aren't too happy when they need a new engine 2 miles down the road.  He also told me one time a guy filled the car with oil while it was RUNNING, without a funnel, and some of it spilled onto the manifolds causing a fire.  Worst part was the manager tried to cover it up and send the customers on there merry way without them knowing, but the husband figured out something wasn't right when he noticed a burning smell and the manager being extra nice.  <P>||||reg||10
Z||000019||Tigger||03-03-2001||10:10 PM||||Let me add one more Pep Boys story.<P>I bought new plugs and wires from them.  The plugs were fine, the wires were for the DIS engine.  Heck, the longest wire in the box was shorter than the shortest wire for my 4 cyl!<P>As soon as I realized they gave me the wrong wires I said something like $h!T, this won't work.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>BTW, that store has went out of business.||||reg||13
Z||000020||wahoo4u||03-04-2001||08:14 PM||||You would be suprised how nice it is to have somebody in a parts house that know fieros.  I am one.  So far I have gotten calls from another store as far as 2 hours away, because the counter guy didn't know much about them.  I didn't know that there was this many fieros around my area until the word got out that the owner of one worked at a parts house.  I have even had people ask who owned the fiero outside, just so they could talk to me.  So yes, it is a true pleasure to help out.  I have been to other parts houses before i got my job, and nobody seems to know anything.||||reg||1
Z||000021||FieroJoe||03-04-2001||09:27 PM||||luckily, I havent had that much trouble with parts, yet, *knock on wood*.  The only annoying thing that gets me is when I call my local NAPA store, the first thing out of their mouths is "Thank you for calling NAPA, can you hold?".  I usually do, becuase they have been the cheapest for a few things.  But after a while, it gets damn annoying.<P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000022||Wolfhound||03-05-2001||05:58 AM||||wahoo4u<BR>I went to a Advance Auto Parts (I Think) in Huntsville. I told the guy I needed a waterpump for a Fiero.<BR>The guy said "A four or a six?"<BR>I told him and he walked off and got it. It turns out he had a Formula.||||reg||14
Z||000023||MontanaFiero||03-06-2001||01:37 PM||||Then there's Checker...<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><P><LI>"Yeah, I need a headlight for an '87 Fiero"<BR><LI><I>"2.5 or 2.8?"</I><BR><LI>"It doesn't matter"<BR><LI><I>"Well, I have to put it in the computer anyway"</I><BR><LI>"2.5"<BR><LI><I>"Auto or Manual?"</I><BR><LI><B>What?!?!"</B> It's just a Fricken headlight!<BR><LI><I>"Would you like oil with that?"</I><BR></UL><p>[This message has been edited by MontanaFiero (edited 03-06-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000024||N_Man||03-06-2001||03:38 PM||||heh, Dumb people at part stores... Well all of the major canadian chains seem to like dumb people as well.  <BR>I have a few good stories but im gonna be the positive guy on this thread.<P>There is a local store that my dad has gone to for years, I rarely went to them till about a year ago because they are out of the way.  But when i went in i was greeted by an older guy that was happy to help.  Later i want back with my dad and they greeted him with his first name and asked how his alfa was running.  Since then I've been going there for most of my part, and when i walk in i get greeted with how is the fiero  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Well i couldnt be happier with the guys at superier automotive.  Try some of the local shops you guys might be really impressed.||||reg||1
Z||000025||stsmithgt||03-06-2001||05:51 PM||||Hay HAZE,  At least they had the part in stock if they knew it or not and you need a bigger clip on that virtual gun of yours.  It would save on reloading time. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||3
Z||000026||Roy Grooms||03-06-2001||07:01 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by sqoach:<BR><B>haze, i'm replacing my ignition lock thingy too. i've gotten all the way down to the lock plate, but can't get it off of there. i know there's a special tool to use to get that off of there. when you get it installed, just give an update as to how difficult it was to do. thanks.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE>its not too hard there is a scew be hand the turn signal thats eazy to miss. also you may have to replace the snap ring, i had to replace mine when the key snapped off. and couldn't get the rest of the key out<P><BR>||||reg||7
Z||000027||Cheever2||03-06-2001||07:37 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MontanaFiero:<BR><B>"It doesn't matter"</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE>I needed wiper blade refills & went back to the parts store that treated me right when I needed a heater core (O'Reilly's - sp).  He asked "what year"... correct me if I'm wrong, but don't all years have the same size wiper blades?<BR> <P>||||reg||6
Z||000028||DJRice||03-06-2001||10:59 PM||||Discount Auto Parts:<P>Me:  I need a set of rear brake pads for an 87 Fiero with the V6 engine.<P>Clerk #1:  I had a friend with a Fiero...He had to use starting fluid every morning to get the darn thing started, but after it ran like a top.  <P>Me: That's Odd.  &lt;thinking to myself, I just use my ignition key&gt;<P>Clerk #1:  What engine?  <P>Me: Six Cylinder.<P>Clerk #2:  Did you say you have a Fiero?<P>Me: Yep<P>Clerk #1:  Front or Rear Pads?<P>Me: Rear<P>Clerk #2:  Is it true that you have to pull the engine out to change the spark plugs?<P>Me:  Only if you have the V6 and want to change all six plugs...<P>Clerk #2:  That sucks.  <P>Me:  I wasnt serious...<P>Clerk #1:  Here you go. Better you than me working on that thing.<P>Me:  No doubt...<P><P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6||||reg||1
Z||000029||mope||03-06-2001||11:03 PM||||a guy i went to school with had his brakes done at pepboys. new lines, master and everything. they must have been out of brake fluid so they just put motor oil in instead. well after that he just said Fu©k it and junked the car. (dont know what kind of car it was)<P>mope||||reg||1
